        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.372,
            0.881,
            0.408
          ],
          "content": "**Q3. How many fractions lie between 0 and 1? Think, discuss with your classmates, and write your answer.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.417,
            0.452,
            0.435
          ],
          "content": "Ans. Uncountable number of fractions"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.444,
            0.882,
            0.528
          ],
          "content": "**Q4. What is the length of the blue line and black line shown below? The distance between 0 and 1 is 1 unit long, and it is divided into two equal parts. The length of each part** is ${ \\frac { 1 } { 2 } } .$ So the blue line is $\\frac { 1 } { 2 }$ **units long. Write the fraction that gives the length of the black line in the box.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.537,
            0.197,
            0.567
          ],
          "content": "Ans. $\\frac { 3 } { 2 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.576,
            0.854,
            0.595
          ],
          "content": "**Q5. Write the fraction that gives the lengths of the black lines in the respective boxes.**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.602,
            0.261,
            0.634
          ],
          "content": "Ans. $\\frac{6}{5}, \\frac{7}{5}, \\frac{8}{5}, \\frac{9}{5}$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.118,
            0.641,
            0.249,
            0.662
          ],
          "content": "**Section 7.5**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.672,
            0.236,
            0.69
          ],
          "content": "**Page No. 162**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.117,
            0.699,
            0.233,
            0.717
          ],
          "content": "**Figure it out**"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.726,
            0.486,
            0.757
          ],
          "content": "**Q1. How many whole units are there in** $\\frac { 7 } { 2 } ?$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.765,
            0.412,
            0.796
          ],
          "content": "Ans. There are 3 whole units in $\\frac { 7 } { 2 }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.804,
            0.562,
            0.836
          ],
          "content": "**Q2. How many whole units are there in** $\\frac{4}{3}$ **and in** $\\frac { 7 } { 3 } ?$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.116,
            0.843,
            0.589,
            0.876
          ],
          "content": "Ans. There is 1 whole unit in $\\frac{4}{3}$ and 2 whole units in $\\frac { 7 } { 3 } .$"
        }
      ]
    }
